{title: I’m just warming up}

{comment: Chorus}
I’m just warming up, I’m just warming up
I’m just warming up for that meeting in the sky
And if you think I’m strange, don’t wait for me to change
I’m just warming up till I’ve reached the other side

{comment: Verse 1}
I went to visit a church and it was quiet as could be
There was nobody praising the Lord, nobody but me
They said I was emotional, I felt out of place
But when I come to church I don’t just come to take up space

{comment: Verse 2}
When I reach those pearly gates, they swing open wide
I’m gona leap for joy for I’ve reached to other side
All my pain and sorrow, there I will forget
And if you think I’ve shout down here, you ain’t seen nothing yet
